const meanings={
p007:['Prioritize confirmed active destruction while preserving feasible evidence and continuing assessment.','Qualified bounded main and all three alternative rationales. The supplied active encryption warrants urgent response relative to these other findings; failed logins and missing patches are not declared harmless. No universal first containment step, completed response or confirmed absence of other compromise is inferred.','The unsupported hotspot metadata still calls the expected firewall-update alert a firmware update; that hidden label is not used by the current choice UI/grader and is not approved by this feedback-only judgment.'],
p008:['Separate safe username lookup from salted password verification and session creation.','Qualified bounded main and all three alternative rationales under the supplied illustrative pseudocode. The input concatenation introduces the injection flaw; connection/execution alone are not the stated root cause. Parameter binding for the username value and subsequent password verification are teaching proposals, not an executed exploit, secure session audit or deployed authentication fix.','The existing whole-choice HOTSPOT grammar has no trusted revision; identifying one index supplies no independent authentication or query-construction mastery.'],
p022:['Interpret the explicitly stipulated unmanaged IaaS compute boundary without generalizing to every cloud service.','HOLD full bundle: the fourth offered choice is application code but its alternative rationale retains a contrast with IAM. Retained hotspot labels/diagram positions also describe application data and IAM where the revised choice list offers runtime and application code. A correct main paragraph does not align every current choice/rationale association.','Provider responsibility for the hypervisor is conditional on this stated agreement; managed services and actual contracts may allocate responsibilities differently. No new parent disposition or real cloud assessment.'],
p030:['Document evidence handover continuity under the stated handling procedure.','Qualified bounded main and all three alternative rationales for the fictional log. Missing documented transfer is the illustrated continuity gap. A modern hash need not be MD5; documented images/copies support preservation without proving legal admissibility. Required acknowledgements depend on the applicable procedure, and authorized live acquisition may interact with the source.','The captured snapshot is reconciled before effective editorial feedback; no captured sentence, universal signature requirement, actual forensic collection or court outcome is approved.'],
p056:['Distinguish access-decision models and recognize their overlap and implementation constraints.','HOLD full delivered bundle: five source-specific blank explanations and five option definitions appear in practice but are omitted from completed Exam review. DAC owner discretion, mandatory central policy, role permissions, attribute evaluation and rule conditions are readable source teaching; the main paragraph alone is not full feedback.','Models can combine; ABAC can implement discretionary/mandatory policies, rule conditions are not exclusive to one model, and Zero Trust is broader than ABAC. No control implementation or most-secure ranking.'],
p067:['Distinguish envelope-source authorization, signed content and visible-From alignment.','HOLD full delivered bundle: three part explanations and three definitions are present in source/practice but missing from completed Exam review. DMARC needs an aligned pass from either SPF or DKIM, not necessarily both; DKIM signing is not encryption and a pass does not establish a trustworthy human sender.','Current RFC9989 introduction confirms the bounded aligned-pass semantics. No DNS changes, actual mail validation, reporting pipeline or full protocol conformance assessment.'],
p079:['Compare endpoint controls by protection context and coverage limits.','HOLD full delivered bundle: five part explanations and five definitions are omitted in completed Exam review. The source distinguishes locked-device storage protection, behavior monitoring/response, execution policy, connection filtering and addressed vulnerabilities.','Protected keys/device state matter; an unlocked authorized session, abuse of allowed tools/ports and unknown or non-vulnerability access methods remain different risks. No endpoint command, configuration, tested control or prevention guarantee.']};
